75,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_mcp_health.py:16-18 docstring: '/health is a FastMCP custom_route ... OUTSIDE the SDK RequireAuthMiddleware ... so an unauthenticated container HEALTHCHECK/probe still gets 200 even when auth is enabled'","register_health_route (_mcp_health.py:295-308) returns JSONResponse({'in_flight':..., 'store': store_status()}) with no auth","Plan AC3: 'reports a DEGRADED opcert field and logs a boot WARNING' — placement (public /health body vs. boot log only) and field contents are left unspecified, whereas AC1's WARNING contents are explicitly named","ANTI-FP note: key paths and the public principal/trusted_env keys are non-secret, so this is an undeclared-posture ambiguity, not a secret-leak (no HIGH class fires)"],"finding":"AC3 adds a DEGRADED `opcert` field to the MCP health surface (`_mcp_health.py`), whose existing `/health` route is deliberately unauthenticated and network-reachable (registered outside RequireAuthMiddleware), but the plan does not declare whether that degraded field is exposed on the unauthenticated `/health` JSON body reachable by a lower-trust probe or confined to boot logs, nor what the field contains.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fce35e0a4ac69367c","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / AC3 (`the MCP server's existing health surface (src/rebar/_mcp_health.py)`)","norm_id":"ncda0fe6d48583d32","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An unauthenticated probe scrapes /health and reads the degraded opcert field, learning that the box's signer is unpinned/mismatched — operational reconnaissance on a pre-existing public route"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In AC3, state explicitly that the degraded signal is either (a) confined to the boot WARNING log plus an authenticated/internal readiness path, OR (b) a boolean/enum status field on public /health carrying no key material (no key path), matching the existing non-sensitive in_flight/store fields — and record the deliberate public-with-rationale choice.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the mint-time guard is best-effort: if `_read_opcert_pub(key_path)` fails/raises, the guard emits a WARNING (or is silent) and sign_manifest still returns the signature, never propagating the guard's own error into the sign path.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.734,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'it still returns the signature (no refusal, no existing sign flow broken)'","Approach step 1: 'read THAT key's own public line with `_read_opcert_pub(key_path)`' — no stated behavior if that read raises","Testing specifies startup-side 'a resolution fault is surfaced as degraded (not swallowed)' but the mint-side probe's own failure mode is unspecified"],"finding":"The mint-time guard's own probe (`_read_opcert_pub(key_path)`) could itself fail (unreadable key path, malformed pub line), but the plan does not specify that the guard must be best-effort and must not propagate its own errors into the sign path — which would contradict AC1's 'no existing sign flow broken'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4f3492073645c08a","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / AC1","norm_id":"n49625f0383d64a70","priority":0.066,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The resolved signing key path exists (ensure_opcert_key succeeded) but `_read_opcert_pub` raises on a transient read/parse error during the guard — if unhandled, sign_manifest crashes instead of signing"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add to Approach step 1 and AC1: wrap the guard probe so any failure to read/parse the signing key's own pub degrades to a warning and never aborts the mint.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Classify the `sign_opcert_manifest` minting seam explicitly (in-scope: add the same specific-key membership warning; or out-of-scope with a stated rationale) so the guard's coverage of every mint path is unambiguous.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5643,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'after `ensure_opcert_key` resolves the SPECIFIC signing key path used for this mint … check whether it is a MEMBER of the verify-side resolvable set'","`ensure_opcert_key` is called only in `mint_opcert_record` (src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:320); `sign_manifest` reaches it via `_sign_manifest_under_lock` → `_prepare_manifest_event` (signing.py:218).","`sign_opcert_manifest` (src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:586) takes `key_path` as a parameter and mints via `opcert.sign_opcert(...)` directly — it never calls `ensure_opcert_key`, so a guard placed there is not exercised.","`sign_opcert_manifest` is a public re-export ('Re-exported as `rebar.signing.sign_opcert_manifest`') consumed outside `_opcert_signing.py` (src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py:86)."],"finding":"The plan's mint-time guard is scoped to the `sign_manifest` path (which mints via `mint_opcert_record` where `ensure_opcert_key` resolves the key), but a second independent public minting seam — `sign_opcert_manifest` (src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:586, re-exported as `rebar.signing.sign_opcert_manifest`, consumed by `_commands/remote_cert.py` and the opcert test suite) — mints a DSSE op-cert under a CALLER-SUPPLIED `key_path` without calling `ensure_opcert_key` or `mint_opcert_record`, so it is NOT covered by the specified guard and can still silently mint an uncertifiable cert. The plan neither enumerates this sibling seam nor classifies it in/out-of-scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb5dcc01cef544cec","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / AC1 / Scope","norm_id":"n694d657aabf82bc2","priority":0.2357,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caller mints via `sign_opcert_manifest` (e.g. remote-cert / test flows) under a key whose public half is not in `_opcert_own_public_keys`: no warning fires because the guard only sits in `mint_opcert_record`."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State whether `sign_opcert_manifest` is in scope; if in scope, place the membership check on the resolved/passed `key_path` in both mint seams (or in the shared `opcert.sign_opcert` wrapper) rather than solely after `ensure_opcert_key` in `mint_opcert_record`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify that AC3's pinned-key MATCH retains the derivation of the bound signer's own public key (via _read_opcert_pub/_derive_opcert_pub) and that only a standalone can-we-derive-a-pub probe is out of scope, so the two are not confused.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6868,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a redundant derive probe' is Out of scope because '_derive_opcert_pub ... re-derivable on demand' makes a resolve/derive probe REDUNDANT","Plan AC3: the non-redundant condition is 'whether the bound signer's public key MATCHES the environment's pinned/published trusted-environment key' — which requires obtaining the bound signer's public key, i.e. reading/deriving it","Code: trusted_env_keyring returns records with 'public_key'; comparing requires the signer's own pub line, obtained via _read_opcert_pub/_derive_opcert_pub"],"finding":"AC3's pinned-key match necessarily derives the bound signer's public key (to compare its type+base64 body against the trusted_env keyring's public_key), yet 'a redundant derive probe' is listed Out of scope on the rationale that derivation is redundant; the plan does not explicitly reconcile that the derivation feeding the MATCH is retained while only a standalone derive-only probe is excluded.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd31597f435e26f06","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / AC3 reframing / Scope (Out of scope: 'a redundant derive probe')","norm_id":"n4a3268237ed9e3d2","priority":0.1132,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer reads 'no derive probe' out-of-scope and hesitates to derive the bound signer's pub at all, leaving AC3 unable to perform the match","A read-only secrets mount where the .pub cache cannot be written: the match must still derive from the private key (as _derive_opcert_pub's docstring notes) — the plan should confirm this derivation is in scope"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In the Scope note, distinguish: 'Out of scope: a standalone can-we-derive-a-public-key startup probe (redundant, per AC3). IN scope: deriving the bound signer's own public line solely to compare its type+base64 body against the pinned trusted_env key — the non-redundant match.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"f6a1e6711bcf01a1","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["ba2dbd4661888f1a",6698],"description_boxes":["90a512a5b8a10706",0],"file_impact":["0d78022b2ab25aea",3],"ticket_id":["825fb4bdbfc7d6f3",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":2786.7,"input_tokens":1105761,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":256008.4,"output_tokens":23038,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":264246.5,"verify_requests":16},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.